A||N||17||MotherGoose||ECM Trouble?||||5||
Z||000000||MotherGoose||05-08-2000||10:47 AM||||I just bought an 87 GT.  I had it runnig Ok but it needed a new alternator.  I put it in and drove it about 10 Miles, then it just died,(like it ran out of gas.)  I self tested the ECM with a paper clip, but the CHECK ENGINE light didn't blink at all.  Does this mean that the ECM is blown?  If so would that keep my car from starting?<P>Thanks  Goose||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||05-08-2000||11:18 AM||||Does the <B>Check Engine</B> light come on at all when you turn on the ignition?||||reg||5
Z||000002||MotherGoose||05-08-2000||11:26 AM||||No...It used to before it died.  But since it quit, it doesn't come on at all.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||05-08-2000||12:44 PM||||I would check fuses first before changing ECM. GM cars use what they call a "floating" ground. If a fuse blows sometimes other things will light up due to this floating ground set-up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MotherGoose||05-08-2000||12:58 PM||||All the fuses in the fuse box are fine, should I look for some others else where?<P>And if the ECM were bad would it keep the car from starting?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||05-08-2000||03:42 PM||||Yes, if the ECM doesn't work your car will not start. But before swapping the ECM, do a few simple checks first.<P>First I would suggest to reset the computer. It <B>is</B> a computer, so it <B>can</B> crash. Just remove the ground cable from your battery for 5 minutes. Reconnect it, and try to start the car. Next, check the Check Engine light bulb.<P>Perhaps you can also tell us exactly what happens when you try to start the car: does any indicator light up when you turn the ignition? Can you hear the fuel pump for approx. 2 seconds? Does the engine turn? Does it sound like it's <B>almost</B> about to start? Do you smell gas fumes? Do you smell something else? Any smoke coming from the exhaust?||||reg||1
Z||000006||MotherGoose||05-08-2000||04:09 PM||||OK heres the poop...Everything works, radio, turn signals, windows, everything.  I am getting spark and the wires and plugs are new.  I pressed the schader valve in after trying to start it, and a small burst of gas comes out, so it should be getting gas.  However, when I try to start it, it sounds like its not getting spark or gas.  The engine turns but it just doesn't kick over.  It doesn't even kick a little bit, it just keeps turning.  <P>I did take the battary out to charge it up, and when I put it back it, the engine light still didn't come on.<P>I hope it is the ECM and not something strange.<P>Thanks for the help so far<P>MotherGoose||||reg||1
Z||000007||MotherGoose||05-08-2000||04:27 PM||||Oh Yeah...The Check Engine light does not come on when I turn the ignition on.  It doesn't come on at all any more.<P>MotherGoose||||reg||4
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||05-08-2000||04:33 PM||||If you turn the ignition to the <B>on</B> position, can you hear the fuel pump for 2 seconds? If I remember correctly, it's the ECM who's responsible for switching it on prior to starting.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Homicidal||05-08-2000||04:53 PM||||Here's a long shot, but it sounds VERY similiar to what happened to me.  Check the Ignition Control Module.  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||MotherGoose||05-08-2000||06:37 PM||||I have already changed the Ignition Control Module, that was the first thing I replaced.  When I turn over to ignition I hear a slight click in the passanger rear area, but thats it.  I also just checked for the Service Engine light again, and no dice.  It never came on.<P>Thanks for everyones imput<P>MotherGoose||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cliff Pennock||05-08-2000||07:23 PM||||That click isn't the fuel pump. The fuel pump makes a "whirrrrrr" sound for 2 seconds. It <I>does</I> sound like the ECM is shot (or the fuelpump).||||reg||1
Z||000012||daved||05-08-2000||11:30 PM||||Mother...Check your email for a chart that may help.  Let us know how you get on, dave<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||MotherGoose||05-09-2000||01:00 AM||||Thank you everyone, tomorrow I'm going to by an ECM and see if that works, I can always return it if it doesn't do the trick.<P>But again thanks everyone, and I'll keep you posted<P>MotherGoose||||reg||1
Z||000014||Ozzy||05-09-2000||02:34 AM||||Another "shot in the dark" but relevant...<P>When I got my '87 GT I noticed sometimes it would die. I did not trust the fuel guage and coincedently it was low on gas when this happened several times. The fuse box was hanging down and while I had the engine running I got in and accidently kicked the fuse box and the engine died abruptly. I thought of a loose connection down there somwhere. Upon further investigation, I wiggled the fuses. When I wiggled the ECM fuse, the engine would die. The fuse was good and would check for power on both blades but the problem was corrosion on the fuse blades themselves. A quick cleanup with a small wire brush fixed that real quick!<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000015||MotherGoose||05-09-2000||10:22 AM||||I have noticed that the fuses in the panel seem a little loose.  I have replaced all of them with new ones, but they seem to kind of hang down a little.  They don't fall out, but they don't seem to stay all the way up like my other car.<P>Thanks<P>MotherGoose||||reg||4
Z||000016||stsmithgt||05-10-2000||12:38 PM||||I may have missed something, but could it possibly be a problem with the pick-up coil in the distributor or the coil itself since they seem to just go out while going down the road???  Everything still works except the dang car won't start right?  Just my two cents if I dug it out of the right pocket of info. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000017||MotherGoose||05-10-2000||12:42 PM||||I'm getting plenty of spark, it just died going down the road.  and hasn't started since.<P>Goose||||reg||1
